## 🔄 End-to-End Flow Analysis

### Flow 1: Auth → Dashboard

```
Login Page → POST /api/auth/login → verify_password (PBKDF2) → create_token (JWT)
    → cookie set (document.cookie, not httpOnly) → middleware.ts (cookie check)
    → GET /api/auth/me → sidebar renders user info
```

> [!WARNING]
> **JWT stored in non-httpOnly cookie** — accessible via JavaScript, vulnerable to XSS. For SaaS release, should use `httpOnly` + `Secure` flags server-side.

### Flow 2: Inbound Call

```
Twilio webhook → POST /incoming-call → validate Twilio signature
    → return TwiML (WebSocket connect) → /media-stream WS
    → parse_telephony_websocket → load_agent(agent_id)
    → build Pipeline: Transport → STT → StateMachine → LLM → TransitionFilter → TTS
    → greeting via TTSSpeakFrame → conversation loop
    → call_logger.start_call() → live_monitor.emit("call_started")
    → on each user utterance: transcript logged + context injected
    → on LLM [TRANSITION: x]: state machine advances
    → on [HANGUP]: EndFrame pushed, call ends
    → finally: call_logger.end_call() → db_persist_call()
```

> [!CAUTION]
> **`register_tools_for_agent()` sets module-level globals** `_current_call_sid` and `_current_agent_config`. With concurrent calls, Call B overwrites Call A's context. Tools like `book_appointment` then log leads under the **wrong tenant**.

### Flow 3: Campaign Dialer

```
POST /api/campaigns/{id}/start → load_campaign → CampaignDialer(max_concurrent)
    → asyncio.create_task(_dial_loop) → for each contact:
        → check schedule (business hours) → semaphore acquire
        → _make_call: update status → Twilio API create call
            → calls /incoming-call?agent_id=X&outbound=1&contact_name=Y
        → 30s wait between calls → retry failed once after 5min
    → mark campaign completed
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Each `_make_call` does `load_campaign` + `save_campaign` (full campaign including all contacts) under a lock. For campaigns with 1000+ contacts, this serializes a large JSON payload on every single call. Works for small campaigns but won't scale.

### Flow 4: Monitor WebSocket

```
Dashboard monitor page → useCallMonitor hook
    → ws://localhost:8765/ws/monitor (NO AUTH)
    → receives: call_started, call_ended, transcript, state_transition
    → sends: {action: "subscribe", call_id: "..."} for transcript detail
    → live_monitor.broadcast_event sends to ALL connections (no tenant filter)
```

> [!CAUTION]
> No authentication on the WebSocket. No tenant scoping on broadcasts. Any client gets all tenants' data.

