## 🟠 High Severity Issues (P1)

### 6. Hardcoded `localhost:8765` in 3 Frontend Files

| File | Line | Issue |
|---|---|---|
| [useCallMonitor.ts:37](file:///Users/maftaalif/Documents/Superactive/dashboard/src/hooks/useCallMonitor.ts#L37) | `ws://localhost:8765/ws/monitor` | Breaks in production |
| [useCallMonitor.ts:104](file:///Users/maftaalif/Documents/Superactive/dashboard/src/hooks/useCallMonitor.ts#L104) | `http://localhost:8765/api/calls/` | Hardcoded takeover URL |
| [Sidebar.tsx:27](file:///Users/maftaalif/Documents/Superactive/dashboard/src/components/Sidebar.tsx#L27) | `http://localhost:8765/api/auth/me` | Should use `API_BASE_URL` |

**Fix:** Use `API_BASE_URL` from `lib/api.ts` everywhere. Derive WebSocket URL from it.

---

### 7. No Rate Limiting on Auth Endpoints

No rate limiting on `/api/auth/login` or `/api/auth/register`. Combined with PBKDF2 600k iterations, brute-force attacks = CPU exhaustion.

**Fix:** Add `slowapi` rate limiter.

---

### 8. Column Injection in Dynamic DB Updates

**File:** [db.py:233](file:///Users/maftaalif/Documents/Superactive/db.py#L233)

```python
sets = ", ".join(f"{k} = ?" for k in fields)  # Column names from caller
```

`db_update_tenant()`, `db_update_campaign_fields()`, `db_update_contact()` all accept arbitrary `**fields` and interpolate column names directly into SQL.

**Fix:** Whitelist allowed column names per function.

---

### 9. JWT in Non-HttpOnly Cookie

**File:** [login/page.tsx:36](file:///Users/maftaalif/Documents/Superactive/dashboard/src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx#L36)

```typescript
document.cookie = `superactive_auth=${token}; path=/; max-age=259200; SameSite=Lax`;
```

No `Secure` flag, no `httpOnly`. Token is accessible to any JavaScript on the page (XSS vector).

**Fix:** Set cookie server-side with `httpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict`.

---

### 10. No WebSocket Reconnection Logic

**File:** [useCallMonitor.ts](file:///Users/maftaalif/Documents/Superactive/dashboard/src/hooks/useCallMonitor.ts)

If the WebSocket disconnects (network flap, server restart), the monitor page goes dead with no auto-reconnect. Users must manually refresh.

**Fix:** Add exponential backoff reconnection (common pattern: retry at 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, max 30s).

---

### 11. Default Admin Password is "admin"

**File:** [db.py:838](file:///Users/maftaalif/Documents/Superactive/db.py#L838)

Migration creates default admin with password `"admin"`. If deployed without changing it, any attacker can log in.

**Fix:** Force password change on first login, or generate a random password and print to logs.

