## 🎨 Frontend / Tailwind CSS Transition

### Current State

The dashboard already uses **Tailwind CSS v4** (imported via `@import "tailwindcss"` in `globals.css`), but it's used in a **hybrid pattern**:

1. **`globals.css`** (304 lines) — Custom CSS classes: `.glass-card`, `.sidebar`, `.btn-primary`, `.badge-*`, `.data-table`, `.input`, `.metric-card`, `.toggle-switch`, etc.
2. **Pages/Components** — Mix of Tailwind utility classes (`className="flex items-center gap-4"`) AND inline styles (`style={{ display: "flex", gap: 12 }}`) AND custom CSS classes (`.glass-card`)
3. **package.json** already includes `tailwind-merge` and `clsx` — merge utilities are ready

### Recommendation: Full Tailwind Transition

> [!TIP]
> **You're already 60% there.** Tailwind v4 is installed and actively used. The transition is about eliminating the 304-line `globals.css` and converting inline styles to utility classes — not a ground-up rewrite.

**Migration Strategy:**

| Phase | Scope | Effort |
|---|---|---|
| **Phase 1** | Convert all inline `style={{}}` to Tailwind utilities | ~2 hours |
| **Phase 2** | Replace `.glass-card`, `.btn-*`, `.badge-*` with `@apply` or component classes | ~1 hour |
| **Phase 3** | Define design tokens as Tailwind CSS custom theme (replace CSS variables) | ~1 hour |
| **Phase 4** | Remove `globals.css` entirely (except scrollbar + animations) | ~30 min |

**Before:**
```tsx
<div style={{ display: "flex", justifyContent: "space-between", alignItems: "center", marginBottom: 28 }}>
```

**After:**
```tsx
<div className="flex justify-between items-center mb-7">
```

**Custom classes → Tailwind `@apply`:**
```css
/* Keep in globals.css but use Tailwind primitives */
.glass-card {
  @apply bg-gray-900/70 backdrop-blur-xl border border-gray-700/50 rounded-2xl transition-all duration-200;
}
```

**Key benefit:** Eliminates the current **3 competing styling systems** (inline, custom CSS classes, Tailwind utilities) into one consistent approach.

