## 🧪 Testing Assessment & Plan

### Current State: Zero Automated Tests

The `scripts/` directory contains **7 manual one-off test scripts** — none use a test framework:

| Script | Purpose | Is it automated? |
|---|---|---|
| `test_agent_config.py` | Loads debug_chat agent, initializes LLM | ❌ Manual, `pass` in test body |
| `test_tool_wrapper.py` | Tests FunctionCallParams reconstruction | ❌ Manual mock, no assertions |
| `test_search.py` | Tests Tavily search | ❌ Manual |
| `test_tavily_direct.py` | Direct Tavily API test | ❌ Manual |
| `reproduce_search_fail.py` | Debug script | ❌ Manual |
| `trigger_call.py` | Initiates a test call | ❌ Manual |
| `verify_superbowl.py` | Verifies search results | ❌ Manual |

**No test framework installed** (no `pytest` in `requirements.txt`). No CI/CD pipeline.

### Recommended Test Strategy

#### Tier 1: Unit Tests (pytest, ~20 tests)

| Test Suite | Covers | Priority |
|---|---|---|
| `test_auth.py` | `hash_password`, `verify_password`, `create_token`, `decode_token`, `get_current_user` | P0 |
| `test_state_machine.py` | `ConversationMemory`, repeat detection, frustration detection, limit checks, state transitions | P0 |
| `test_agent_config.py` | `AgentConfig` validation, `build_full_prompt()`, guardrail levels | P1 |
| `test_db.py` | All CRUD operations (tenant, user, agent, campaign, call, lead), migration | P1 |
| `test_tool_registry.py` | `get_tools_for_agent`, tool handler responses | P1 |

#### Tier 2: Integration Tests (~10 tests)

| Test | Covers |
|---|---|
| Auth flow | Register → Login → Token → Protected endpoint |
| Agent CRUD | Create → Read → Update → Delete with tenant isolation |
| Campaign lifecycle | Create → Upload CSV → Start → Pause → Resume |
| Call logging | start_call → add_transcript → end_call → db_persist |

#### Tier 3: E2E Browser Tests (~5 tests)

| Test | Covers |
|---|---|
| Login flow | Navigate to `/login` → enter credentials → redirected to dashboard |
| Agent management | Create agent → verify in list → edit → delete |
| Monitor page | Connect WS → verify connection status indicator |

#### How to Run (proposed):

```bash
# Install pytest
pip install pytest pytest-asyncio httpx

# Run unit tests
pytest tests/ -v

# Run with coverage
pytest tests/ --cov=. --cov-report=html
```

